WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
September 
Fukui Prefecture 
Fujioka East High School

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:04.850
Track team third-year, Takeuchi Makoto-kun.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:07.060
Congratulations on placing fifth

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.820
in the 5,000 meter race at 
the national tournament.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.860
Second-year, Wataya Arata-kun.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.990
Congratulations on winning the 
individual Class A tournament

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.280
at the National High School 
Karuta Championship.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:20.830
Um...

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.750
What is it?

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.830
Oh, uh...

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:27.580
Need this?

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.540
Um...

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:28.590
<b>What?</b>

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.840
U-Um...

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:31.590
<b>Wh—  What?</b>

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.220
N-Never mind.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.720
<b>What?!</b>

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:37.930
<b>Y-You can do it!</b>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:45.770
N-Next year, I'd really like to play 
in the team tournament at Nationals.

00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.940
So if anyone is interested 
in competitive karuta,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.230
p-please come talk to me.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:57.110
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:57.110 --> 00:00:58.950
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:07.020
Verse 2

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:07.020
The hazed 
early dawn 
light comes 
not from 
the moon

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.600
<i>I said it... I went and said it!</i>

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.020
<i>I'm so done!</i>

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.020
What the heck brought this on?

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.270
Even your ears are red.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.020
Yuu...

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.360
I thought you weren't big on
dragging people into karuta.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:18.070
You played karuta through 
grade school, right?

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.030
Nope! Not happening!

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.830
It's summer of our second year.
We'll be exam students soon.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.540
Seriously, what's gotten into you?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.670
<i>Our world of karuta can only grow because of
team players who keep the game alive, right?</i>

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.010
<i>How far can I really go alone?</i>

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.260
Wataya-kun, I wanted to talk to you
about competitive karuta.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.760
What? Y-You play?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.190
My grandma's been bugging me 
about playing it with her.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:52.810
Could you refer me to
the karuta society you're in?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.020
To keep her sharp

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.150
This is the building where we play.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.450
I'm the PE teacher, Kanno!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.280
Wataya-kun, play a game with me!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:07.160
I haven't played since I won the college 
championship fifteen years ago,

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.370
but naturally, I play Class A karuta!

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.210
I'd be glad to play anytime.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:15.000
Wataya-kun! My older brother sometimes 
says he wants to play karuta again!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:18.210
My mom's a ranked player.

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.470
I think my little sister 
will want to play, too.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.220
My grandpa teaches karuta 
at the community center!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.890
<i>A-Aren't there any </i>students<i> at this 
school who want to play karuta?</i>

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.890
<i>I guess I'm being pretty greedy,</i>

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:34.440
<i>wanting to play against their team.</i>

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:37.020
<i>But still...</i>

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:40.150
<i>It might be hard to build 
a high school team,</i>

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.240
<i>but I can generate interest in karuta.</i>

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.950
<i>This is Fukui.</i>

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.160
September 
Tokyo 
Mizusawa High School

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.580
While you all must be sick of these by now,

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.750
I'm sure you've been thinking 
this through over summer break,

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.170
Fourth Future Plans Questionnaire   
Year 2 Class ___ Name ___________

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.170
First Choice 

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:02.420
so fill out your future plans questionnaire
with realistic goals and turn them in.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.850
Chi-chan, aren't you going to
put down "Queen" this time?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.430
Michiru-chan!

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.520
Oh, that's right.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.270
<b>Kyo-Oshiroi 
Blotting Paper</b>

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.230
Here, souvenir from my family trip.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.270
Thanks...

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:17.690
Kyoto? Why'd you go there when
that's where our class trip is going to be?

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:19.320
To prepare.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.610
<b>Traveling in Kyoto
 Golden Scenery</b>

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.320
I checked out everything I could in order to
make our class's free time a fun time!

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.530
Horikawa!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.700
You should run for student council president!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.330
You're such a good class trip
committee member!

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.960
Michiru-chan, you're amazing

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.960
I know it's because of you that
we got USJ added to the itinerary!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.210
I came up with
the perfect spot for you, too.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.920
<i>The autumn of our class trip,</i>

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.470
<i>and an autumn of karuta.</i>

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.470
<i>Strange...</i>

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.810
<i>I thought they would've made
some kind of progress</i>

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.850
<b>Something like this...</b>

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.640
<i>after spending a night and two days
at Fujisaki's karuta camp...</i>

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:59.150
<i>But the only thing that's grown 
stronger is their rivalry.</i>

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.980
That one was mine!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:01.650
No, it was mine!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:05.150
<b>Olympics</b>

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:05.950
<i>Chihaya-chan giving her all
in practice is nothing new.</i>

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.450
<i>What's changed is...</i>

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.450
<i>Taichi has changed.</i>

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.500
<i>His memorization was always super accurate,</i>

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.750
<i>but it's made him even 
sharper in the second half.</i>

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.920
<i>I'll win. I can win.</i>

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.010
<i>How much of a gap should I aim for?</i>

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:26.130
<i>Should I go for Chihaya's 
one-syllable cards?</i>

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:27.930
<i>Above all...</i>

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.680
<i>It's gotten hard to win
with my left hand.</i>

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:32.930
<i>Wow...</i>

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:35.850
Thank you very much.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.610
One more game, Taichi!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.190
No way, Ayase!

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.780
Play me next, Mashima!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.860
Why you? He's playing me! 
Stick to the order!

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:46.700
The Master qualifiers are coming up!

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:48.490
You only just made Class B, so sit down!

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.620
Snap!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.490
Th-That may be so,

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:55.750
but if I win a tournament somewhere 
by October, I'll reach Class A!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.710
Don't be naive! Class B isn't that easy!

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.170
<i>Winning the individual tournament
at the Nationals—</i>

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.010
<i>going through an entire day undefeated—</i>

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.550
<i>can really change a person, huh?</i>

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.550
It's not impossible! I'll show you!

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:13.560
If I win two tournaments somewhere by October,

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.350
I'll reach Class A, too.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.310
And then come the Master qualifiers...

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.980
He hasn't changed...
In fact, he's worse...

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:25.030
Chihaya, you should stop
playing with your left hand.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:25.900
Huh?

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.820
You don't want to
get too comfortable with it.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.030
Go back to your right hand.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.530
But I'm not allowed to take off
the taping yet...

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:34.450
You can still hold down cards to take them.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:34.950
Huh?

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:35.580
Hanano-san.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.960
You'll play Chihaya next.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:46.590
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.000
<i>Frankly, I don't think playing 
Hanano-san will help me.</i>

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:46.880
<i>The Queen qualifiers are coming up, too...</i>

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.380
<i>So spring ends...</i>

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:55.640
Does your right hand hurt, Ayase-senpai?

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.060
Huh? No.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:59.480
Then go on the attack.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:02.020
I'm not going to stay in 
Class D forever, either!

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.520
I'll win more in the next tournament!

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:08.570
I'm not too interested in karuta,

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.530
but I'm willing to work hard for love.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.240
<i>Even Hanano-san is...</i>

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.910
<i>If Mashima-senpai is focused 
more than ever on karuta,</i>

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.540
<i>then I have to do the same.</i>

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.620
<i>I have to get on his radar!</i>

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.420
<i>I have to see what he's seeing!</i>

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:27.660
<i>...taking karuta seriously.</i>

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:32.890
<i>Three players in Class A
and one in Class B...</i>

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:36.220
<i>That should be more than enough for 
any high school karuta club, but...</i>

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.930
<i>I have to strive for Class B, too!</i>

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.230
Everyone! I have terrible news!

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.740
21   59th Master/57th Queen Tournament East Japan Qualifiers 

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.190
What?!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:54.370
The Master and Queen qualifiers overlap 
with the dates of our class trip!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.620
Mizusawa High School Second-Year Class Trip Schedule 
October 20-23

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.620
Why is it on the 21st?!
 It's usually a week earlier!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:59.240
I hadn't kept an eye out for this!

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.750
Which are we supposed to do?!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.170
You will not be permitted 
to skip the class trip!

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:08.130
Let's play karuta again!

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.340
When?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.220
The Queen match!

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:16.140
When we go to Kyoto, let's wear 
junihitoe together at Shigureden.

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:19.390
Cafeteria today?

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.680
I brought my lunch.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.680
Can I see your notes?

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.980
<i>In last year's High School Championship, 
I passed out and had to withdraw.</i>

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:31.240
<i>This year I got hurt, then had surgery, 
and still can't use my right hand.</i>

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:34.070
<i>I was sure I'd be back in 
the game by October, but now...</i>

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>Does the god of karuta hate me?</i>

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:40.450
<i>It's no surprise she's upset.</i>

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:50.050
Chihaya-chan, when you take off 
your shoes, line them up properly!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:50.460
Huh?

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.920
Oh, sorry...

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.050
Did you know that I've been straightening 
out everyone's shoes all this time

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:56.550
without saying anything?

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.970
Yeah... Thanks.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.890
It's because, when I was little,
my mother told me

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.140
that straightening out other people's shoes

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.690
would bring me one instance of good luck.

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:09.690
After a year and a half straightening 
out the shoes of everyone in the club,

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.110
I've amassed so much good luck that

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.160
I probably have ten times as 
much luck in savings as you do!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.410
L-Luck in savings?!

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.910
I'll straighten them! 
I'll get some good luck!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.660
I was just thinking I didn't have any!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.710
Don't put your hands on a white wall.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.710
Don't step on the edge of a tatami mat.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.590
I love the idea of small actions
building up good fortune.

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:39.090
When you're lost, why not think about
what you want to build up within yourself

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.390
and try making decisions that way?

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:46.560
Well, I'll see you after school, Chihaya-chan.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:47.140
Sure...

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.400
<i>Since I put it that way,</i>

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:56.030
<i>she might end up choosing
the Queen match over the class trip.</i>

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.910
<i>I would miss her,</i>

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:05.910
Mizusawa High School Second-Year Class Trip Schedule 
October 20-23

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:05.910
21   59th Master/57th Queen Tournament East Japan Qualifiers 
21  59th Master/57th Queen Tournament West Japan Qualifiers

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>but if that's what Chihaya-chan
wants to build up...</i>

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.920
What the heck, Nitta? This is hilarious!

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.830
"There is a map of life.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:14.920
Class 2-9 Classical Literature Special 
Summer Break Assignment: 20 Poems

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:12.920
It is not sold at Tsutaya. I cry."

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.130
"I cry"? Really?!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:14.920
What's wrong with it?!

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.470
"I drown in idols, and then, a bog of you.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.680
This sea reminds me that I can't swim."

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.010
Hey, Haruno, did you go to
the beach with your girlfriend?

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:22.810
N-No, I didn't!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.810
"The magpie brought that voice to me.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.980
It will be my good luck charm for karuta."

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.940
Even your poems are about karuta?

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.650
"Why don't my jeans from last year fit?

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.440
I know my legs have not grown longer."

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.240
What a dumb poem!

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:42.700
Those of you laughing are the ones
who were not included in our 20 Poems.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.990
How fortunate you are.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:49.160
Now, to those who took this 
poetry assignment seriously

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.250
and those who are laughing 
at them, I say this:

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.880
Learn the pain of creating something.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:01.800
And once you've learned it,
resolve yourself to show lenience to others.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:06.020
In poetry, in literature... in everything.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:13.810
H-Hey, Mr. Fukusaku!
Whose secondhand saying is that?

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.860
Oh, it's something a former university 
teacher of mine often said.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:18.690
I figured!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.990
You should come up with 
some original material for once.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:26.200
Original material, eh?
I don't have too much of that...

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.620
And you call yourself a Japanese teacher?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.210
Good luck in retired life!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.130
Still, in my mind...

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:36.550
The words of the many who came before me

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:39.210
are the treasures I have 
inherited over the years.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.220
And to pass them along to all of you,

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.220
to sell them secondhand...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.260
is why I became a teacher.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.020
It shouldn't cause you any more pain.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:12:00.280
You can use your right hand now.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.540
<i>Finally...</i>

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:16.790
<i>I can finally play karuta 
with my right hand!</i>

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.340
<i>Ayase-senpai really is amazing...</i>

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:30.350
<b>Round Table</b>

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.060
<i>But she's lacking the boldness
she had before.</i>

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.430
<i>She couldn't use her right hand
for two months,</i>

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:32.480
<i>so I guess it makes sense...</i>

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.230
Thank you very much.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.810
Come on, Taichi! Take this seriously!

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.650
Uh, but... your hand's barely recovered.

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:41.860
What if you hit it and end up hurt again?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:45.200
It'll be fine! I've got spirit!

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.280
Her "spirit"...

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.450
She never talks about the class trip.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:55.540
I wonder what she's going to do 
about the East Japan Qualifiers.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.540
Kana-chan.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.460
I'd like to wear a hakama 
in the Yoshino Tournament.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:01.010
Could you help me put it on?

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:04.720
<i>The Yoshino Tournament...</i>

00:13:05.130 --> 00:13:08.600
<i>A tournament for Class A and B players only,</i>

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.020
<i>held right before the Master
and Queen qualifiers.</i>

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.020
<i>Strong players from
all over Japan will be there.</i>

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:17.650
<i>Arata's sure to be in it, too.</i>

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:22.030
O-Of course! We'll lend you
our newest hakama!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.650
Oh, I don't need a hakama.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.700
That's right. You bought one from us.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:27.660
Yeah.

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:30.910
I need to get better at playing in a hakama.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.700
<i>I can see it...</i>

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:37.330
<i>I can see her boycotting the class trip</i>

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.420
<i>to be in the East Japan Qualifiers.</i>

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.300
I'm worried...

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:47.090
Ayase-san, you will go on 
the class trip, right?

00:13:47.090 --> 00:13:48.180
I'm getting ready!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.970
For which one?!

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:54.600
I'll be in big trouble if only members 
of the karuta club skip the trip...

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:56.980
Ms. Miyauchi, Ms. Miyauchi.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:02.020
No one but the student's homeroom 
teacher is supposed to see these,

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.530
but as her former homeroom teacher 
and karuta adviser, I think you can.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.110
A future plans questionnaire?

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.080
Fourth Future Plans Questionnaire   Name: Ayase Chihaya 
How do I become...

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.210
October

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.210
Kawaguchi Comprehensive 
Cultural Center

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.830
Yoshino Tournament

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:19.830
Class A: 70 players 
Class B: 75 players

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.960
The Fukui Nagumo Society has shown you all
the kind of growth no one's seen in years!

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:28.590
They got matching
 T-shirts this year

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:28.590
Let's mow down East Japan's karuta 
societies as the leaders of West Japan!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.850
My Shiranami Society has grown as well.

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:37.430
A karuta society earns points when their members place well

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:37.430
Not only will we win,
but we'll also take home tons of points!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.060
<b>Playing in Class B</b>

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:41.060
You're both fools! The Suihoku Society's 
gonna take it all this year!

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:44.190
Don't worry, guys! I'll get us started!

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.570
You can sleep, Coach.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.360
Why are you here, Makoto? 
Don't you have exams to prep for?

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:52.490
Made Class A 
with two runner-up
 finishes in Class B

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:52.490
Er, I heard that Cheers and Rion were 
the only ones here from our school...

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:52.490
<b>The two of us
are enough!</b>

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.740
Oh, how pretty!

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:56.330
She looks cute!

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.120
I guess it's not just the management
that wears hakamas.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.960
You look beautiful, Chihaya-chan!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.210
They're even letting us set out
Oe Traditional Clothing pamphlets.

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.960
<b>Oe Traditional Clothing</b>

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.960
<b>Celebrating 120 years 
thanks to our customers</b>

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.960
Isn't it wonderful?

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.050
Mashima-senpai, this is for you!

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.050
<b>Propolis Royal Jelly Miracle Super Energy Drink</b>

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.840
Oh, thanks.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:11.050
Good luck!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:14.260
<i>She's looking out for me, in her own way.</i>

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:17.520
We finally get to play 
in the same tournament!

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:18.560
I've waited so long!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.100
Remember what I said?
An individual match is a team match,

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:23.860
and a team match is an individual match.

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:26.530
Let's prove that to everyone together!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:29.650
Together, we will clobber
every other karuta society in Japan!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.720
That reminds me!
I heard about your class trip.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.950
That bad luck of yours
really runs deep, Eyelashes.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.710
But there's no need to rush.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.250
In all things, you kids 
are just getting started.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.720
Welcome to the world of Class A.

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:58.380
I knew it was you, Arata! 
Did you say something?!

00:15:58.380 --> 00:15:59.440
Er, no...

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:00.510
You did, didn't you?

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:01.760
N-No, I didn't...

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.410
Badmouthing me?

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:05.270
No!

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:06.700
Y...

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.600
You look... pretty in that hakama...

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:20.190
I'm going to win every game 
today in this hakama.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.080
You'd better not lose.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:32.080
Hilarious.

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.280
These mixed-gender tournaments
where men and women play each other

00:16:35.280 --> 00:16:38.940
are much tougher than the Master
and Queen matches and qualifiers.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:40.130
I'll still win!

00:16:40.130 --> 00:16:41.310
Oh? Wanna bet?

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:42.620
Yeah!

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:43.810
No betting, idiot!

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:47.310
Don't run away, club president of 
the school that won the Nationals!

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.180
You'll do, too.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:54.690
Whichever one of us loses first has to skip
the Master qualifiers in two weeks.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:58.960
Fine.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:16:59.590
Good.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:01.230
Not fair, Mashima!

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:03.680
You have the class trip then anyway!

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:07.350
<i>In official tournaments,</i>

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:10.910
<i>players from the same society are unlikely
to be drawn together until the latter rounds.</i>

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:15.790
<i>I'm less likely to be drawn with Taichi
than with Arata or Sudo-san.</i>

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.640
Yamai Makoto 
<b>12</b>
Ayase Chihaya

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.390
<b>I get the feeling he hates me...</b>

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:25.100
<i>Take everything one step at a time.</i>

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.800
<i>One win at a time.</i>

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:35.290
<i>Naniwa Bay, now the flower 
blooms, but for winter</i>

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.280
Wow, Ririka-chan's 
grown up...

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.280
Yikes.
 The Queen
runner-up...

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:43.320
<i>Here comes spring, 
now the flower blooms</i>

00:17:37.530 --> 00:17:38.280
Two club presidents! 
It's the red thread
of fate! Cheers!!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:45.710
Class B Room

00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:45.710
Things seem pretty relaxed 
in the Class B room.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.720
I checked out the Class A room earlier,
and it was way more tense.

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:53.080
I guess it would be,
with the Master qualifiers coming up.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:58.510
<i>Attack... Target the opponent's left!</i>

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:01.020
<i>I know the weakness of right-handed players.</i>

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:04.220
<i>Target the center of his left side,
which he's less conscious of!</i>

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.690
<i>it is as though pearls have been 
strung across the autumn plain</i>

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.690
Thank you very much.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:22.690
<i>I should've known a Class B match
wouldn't be like Class C.</i>

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:25.320
<i>I lost by thirteen cards...</i>

00:18:25.650 --> 00:18:29.040
<i>I'm glad everyone else went 
to watch the Class A matches.</i>

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:32.680
<i>Of course I can't win after 
I just made it to Class B.</i>

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:40.970
<i>No! I made up my mind that 
I wouldn't think that way!</i>

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:43.130
<i>I can't do that! I can't do that!</i>

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:47.920
If I win a tournament somewhere 
by October, I'll reach Class A!

00:18:48.590 --> 00:18:49.650
<i>Class A...</i>

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:52.230
<i>Even if no one else took me seriously,</i>

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:54.640
<i>I had high hopes for myself!</i>

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.480
<i>Don't decide this was a matter of course!</i>

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.140
<i>Be mad! And analyze what happened!</i>

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:08.670
If you keep hitting yourself,

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:11.090
you'll hurt yourself, Desktomu-kun!

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:16.050
H-How are the Class A matches going?

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:22.490
Uh... There are so many matches, 
I didn't know who to root for.

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:25.160
So you were watching the Class B
matches the whole time?

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.580
You said you were going to win,

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:32.720
so I wanted to be there to see it.

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:38.060
But...

00:19:38.890 --> 00:19:42.230
It looks like I'll get to Class B before that.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:44.070
I'll catch up to you in no time!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:47.450
Come on, let's go.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:51.900
<i>I'm not the only one with high hopes for me.</i>

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:55.450
I bet it's getting pretty crazy
in the Class A room.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.030
<i>I'm not the only one watching me.</i>

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:01.260
My lack of practice due to
 studying for entrance exams showed...

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.210
Both Chihaya-chan and the Prez
won their matches!

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.280
Amazing.

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.980
And Porky-kun...

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:07.560
Yoshida Yusei 
<b>20</b>
 Sudo Akito

00:20:08.470 --> 00:20:11.070
<i>The fiercest battle of all, 
right in the first round:</i>

00:20:11.490 --> 00:20:13.630
<i>Porky-kun versus Sudo-san.</i>

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:18.310
<i>What's with this guy? I took a 
ten-card lead in the first half.</i>

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:21.560
<i>Yusei's hanging in there! 
He's sticking with it!</i>

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.370
<i>When I led him by twenty cards last year,</i>

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:27.320
<i>I was impressed that
he actually knew when to give up...</i>

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.980
<i>Don't give up. I can keep fighting.</i>

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:34.070
<i>I can keep struggling 
until the very last card!</i>

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:38.500
<i>You've burned off enough fat 
to pass for lean meat, huh?</i>

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:46.090
<i>Don't keep fighting when 
you're going to lose.</i>

00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:48.990
<i>You tired me out in the first match.</i>

00:20:51.740 --> 00:20:54.620
<i>Yusei... you've grown so much!</i>

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:59.610
<i>Sudo-san is good. He'll be an obstacle.</i>

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:03.200
<i>He's going to be a major obstacle
for my teammates!</i>

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.260
<i>I couldn't win, but I wore 
him down as much as I could.</i>

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.870
<i>One of my teammates is gonna win!</i>

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:12.860
<i>Just watch!</i>

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.250
A team match is an individual match.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:18.380
An individual match is a team match.

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:20.430
<i>I always thought</i>

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:23.740
<i>individual matches were where 
everyone fought on their own</i>

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:27.450
<i>just to try to raise their own levels...</i>

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.510
<i>But they're not.</i>

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:33.910
<i>Individual matches are the real team matches!</i>
